      "id": "ccna-management-protocols",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "CCNA",
      "topic": "Remote administration",
      "unit": "management-policy-foundations",
      "title": "Keep remote administration on SSH version 2",
      "summary": "Repair incoming protocol and version policy consistently across supplied terminal lines.",
      "objective": "Allow Admin (192.0.2.10) and Operator (192.0.2.11) to reach the supplied Branch management endpoint at 10.0.0.2 using SSH version 2 on every supplied VTY line, 0–15. Disable Telnet on those lines and reject the supplied legacy SSH version 1 trial. Keep the supplied IP routes and host identity unchanged.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 25,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied management path, edit the complete policy and verify required access and rejection."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "Restrict the complete supplied line range to SSH with transport input ssh and restrict the separate global version policy with ip ssh version 2. Keep both administrators reachable. Check configuration proves all lines against version 2, Telnet and legacy-version cases; an eligible policy is not a successful login.",
      "hints": [
        "The document must remain complete. Select the Telnet trial, then Inspect trial; it should report that the line protocol is disabled.",
        "Version 2 remains eligible for authentication; version 1 is denied by the version policy. An IP path is still required for either trial.",
        "The relevant case identifies the first inconsistent VTY line. Repair the document and retry; checking a single selected line alone does not complete the assignment."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-12/configuration_guide/sec/b_1712_sec_9300_cg/secure_shell_version_2_support.html",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-12/configuration_guide/sec/b_1712_sec_9300_cg/configuring_secure_shell__ssh_.html",
