      "id": "ccna-management-source-policy",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "CCNA",
      "topic": "Remote administration",
      "unit": "management-policy-foundations",
      "title": "Restrict management sources without locking out operators",
      "summary": "Replace an overbroad incoming terminal list while retaining two approved administrators.",
      "objective": "Allow Admin (192.0.2.10) and Operator (192.0.2.11) to reach Branch at 10.0.0.2 using SSH version 2 on every supplied VTY line, 0–15. Reject Guest (192.0.2.130) and Nearby (192.0.2.12) through an incoming source access list. Keep Telnet disabled and the supplied SSH version 1 trial rejected. Keep the supplied IP routes and host identity unchanged.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 30,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied management path, edit the complete policy and verify required access and rejection."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "Replace the early broad permit with ordered exact permits for both approved source addresses, and attach the numbered standard list with access-class NUMBER in on every supplied line. Keep the SSH-only transport and version 2 policy. Both approved clients must remain eligible; both other sources must fail at the source-list layer, not because the route or all protocols were disabled.",
      "hints": [
        "A first-match list must permit both .10 and .11. Unmatched clients are denied without adding a permit any.",
        "Both approved sources remain eligible; each unapproved source is denied by the list. Actual trial output clears when the selection or draft changes.",
        "The nearby workstation catches a rule that is too broad. Return to the narrow policy and verify every case before opening the independent assignment."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-12/configuration_guide/sec/b_1712_sec_9300_cg/secure_shell_version_2_support.html",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-12/configuration_guide/sec/b_1712_sec_9300_cg/configuring_secure_shell__ssh_.html",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-12/configuration_guide/sec/b_1712_sec_9300_cg/configuring_ipv4_acls.html"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Checked2026-11-09 against CCNA200-301v1.1/4.8 and Catalyst9300 IOS XE Dublin17.12 guides updated2023-07-28. Bounded policy before authentication: existing virtual IPv4 forward/reply routes to an actual router-local address, supplied host-identity metadata and explicitly supplied VTY lines. No TCP handshake, SSH crypto, password authentication, AAA, privilege assignment, IOS session or real network access. Complete configuration documents support only the disclosed subset; unsupported commands are rejected. Numbered standard incoming terminal lists only (1–99 or1300–1999); no named VTY list, VRF, outbound terminal list or inferred platform defaults. Each case checks every supplied line; source-policy rejection is distinct from a broken route or disabled protocol. Limits:16supplied line records,6clients,8cases,64KiBdocument. Trial observations are transient and are not restored as execution evidence.",
